# WS requests open a socket and play their script against it:
#   send    writes a message (objects and arrays are sent as JSON)
#   receive waits for the next message: `message` is its text, `data` its JSON
#   wait    pauses, close hangs up
# The whole conversation shows up under the response.

### Echo
WS wss://ws.postman-echo.com/raw

> send json({ type: "hello", from: person(1).name, id: uuid() })
> receive 5s
> assert data.type == "hello"
> assert data.from == person(1).name
> send "ping"
> receive 5s
> assert message == "ping"
> close

### Greeting first
WS wss://echo.websocket.org

> receive 5s
> assert message contains "Request served by"
> send "The quick brown fox"
> receive 5s
> assert message == "The quick brown fox"
